  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p>Despite their canine appearance, a cu sith is no simple hound but a terrifying guardian of fey crossings whose baying howl portends mortality's collapse.</p><p><strong>Size</strong> Large</p><p><strong>Melee</strong> <span class=\"pf2-icon\">1</span> jaws, <strong>Damage</strong> 1d8 piercing plus Grab</p><p><strong>Str</strong> +3, <strong>Dex</strong> +2, <strong>Con</strong> +2, <strong>Int</strong> –3, <strong>Wis</strong> +0, <strong>Cha</strong> +1</p><p><strong>Hit Points</strong> 6</p><p><strong>Skill</strong> Intimidation</p><p><strong>Senses</strong> low-light vision, scent (imprecise, 30 feet)</p><p><strong>Speed</strong> 40 feet</p><p><strong>Special</strong> The cu sith can understand Fey but does not speak any languages. They also don't take a –4 circumstance penalty to [[/act demoralize]] targets due to not speaking or sharing languages.</p><p><strong>Support Benefit</strong> Your cu sith barks fearsomely, robbing your foe of their wits. Until the start of your next turn, when you hit and deal damage to a creature within your cu sith's reach, the target is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied 1}.</p><p><strong>Advanced Maneuver</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e-animal-companions.AC-Advanced-Maneuvers.Item.B9xO4pLtRMCSoLNG]{Worrying Doom}</p>"
    },
